 "memory_levels_method": "points significantly slower than the next kept size excluded as interference (latency cannot fall with working set); piecewise-linear BIC fit of log(median latency) on log(size), weights 1/SE^2 with SE = bootstrap SE of the median widened by t(df=reps-1)/z; a level spans >= 2x size and its fitted rise is significantly less than 0.5x the jump at each edge (z = 2-sided 5% Bonferroni over n-1 breakpoints), as are the plain spread of its interior medians and its slope relative to the edge's slope; the edge must step up toward larger sizes; a lone segment must show no detectable rise; neighbours that would pass as one merged level are merged; capacity bracket starts at the last size where no rep already reached the next level and ends at the first size where no rep was still at this level (null if no next level); a bracket covers what these reps showed, it is not a confidence interval for the true capacity",
